                             Installation

To install PBK2DBF, copy PBK2DBF.IMG to any \IMG\ directory.  Using the
<Psion>-J option, install the RunIMG application.

This program was written for and tested on several PBK files from the
AMIA Medical Forum.  If you have difficulty with any particular PBK
files, please contact the author.


                            De-installation

To de-install the program, delete the PBK2DBF.IMG file.


                               Operation

After running, the program displays a dialog with two file choices.
One is the input file (HP 95LX PBK Phone book format), the other is the
output file (a plain Psion DBF containing only string fields).  This
output file should NOT exist.  If it does, it WILL be overwritten (the
user IS warned after accepting the dialog).

Once the files have been selected, conversion takes place, and a count
of records converted is given.

The PBK file only has three fields: Name, Number, Address.  The address
field can contain multiple lines.  This program always converts each
line to a separate field in the DBF.  No labels record is created.  To
add labels, open the file in the Data application and add labels.


